"heptapod@gmail.com" <heptapod@gmail.com> wrote:
> I was completing sokoban and wondered "What if I teleported the items
> out of the reward closets?" Being a lucky sort of valkyrie I had two
> wands of teleportation, one was completely spent by helping me with
> sokoban mistakes but the other was fully charged.
> At the end there were the three reward rooms with a CoMR and a "oR in
> addition to a BoH which I already got in the mines.
>
> Ended up zapping the CoMR and "oR until they were in a corridor that I
> could kick towards the stairs in a single pile.

I already thought about that and tried to get two sokoprizes in
wizmode some time ago. But I wasn't able to pull it off.

But I noticed if you manage to get the sokoprizes off the last sokoban
level, they are yours.

Although I don't remember if I came to the conclusion that it was
impossible or only nearly impossible (I lean towards impossible, but
who knows?).

If it's nearly impossible and you can do it I think it doesn't break
the game gameplay-wise if you can keep two or more sokoprizes.

Chances are when you can pull that stunt off, you already are way past
the point where more than one sokoprize is an advantage and you are
playing "stupid ascension tricks". :)

> Standing over the booty I got the following messages:
>
> m - an amulet of reflection.
> You see a cloak of magic resistance vanishing.
> You hear something popping. n - a cloak of magic resistance.

What happened here was that you got to pick up an item *after* it was
destroyed by the program.

That means UnNetHack read a part of memory that was just deallocated
but because of this part of memory still fresh it could read it like
normal.

You encountered a bug with one the feared "dangling pointers"
(BTW, those are also hallucinatory monsters).

> Reckon if one of the rewards is teleported out then it oughta be
> considered as the player accepting the item.

I think that's not necessary.

> No idea if this works
> with pets who will 'steal' the items and be magic whistled over to a
> convenient pile area.

Pets aren't allowed to pick up sokoprizes.

> Either way thanks for the extra loot!

Well, you weren't able to enjoy it long. :(

